WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.860
Film Courage: Is there a specific structure
you use or prefer for writing scripts?

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.439
Shawn Christensen, co-writer/director of The
Vanishing of Sidney Hall movie: Well it depends

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.439
on the script.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:12.170
For example, right now I started writing a
screenplay (I just started writing a screenplay)

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.350
based on true life stories.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.779
This is my second one I’m in right now and
it’s a whole different experience than the

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.160
other stuff I did which was just original
material.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:31.310
I prefer writing the true story or the stuff
based on real-life stuff because frankly the

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:38.070
people’s stories are better than my imagination.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:44.760
Some of their own stories of what has happened
is better than what I would make up.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.329
And in those cases I have to do a lot of research
and adapt.

00:00:50.329 --> 00:00:54.460
So adapting a script and an original script
are two different things.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:00.239
For an original screenplay I usually start
with the characters and let them talk to each

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:05.290
other and I kind of have an idea of the plot.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:06.540
I don’t outline.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.869
I just let the characters infer the plot.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:15.090
Like I know the concept and I know the overall
beginning, middle and end and I let the characters

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:21.350
decide how we get from the middle and the
end, let them bounce off of each other like

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.560
improvising and then build around that.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:31.460
But for adapting you can’t really do that
so you kind of have to gather all of the facts

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:38.840
and do all of the research and then it’s
honestly something I’m learning to be honest.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:45.100
I really just kind of writing out all of the
things (the great moments) in this particular

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:50.030
script I’m writing and then knowing that
I’m going to cut half of them out.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.619
But just really I write them out because they
are fun, they’re great, they are interesting

00:01:54.619 --> 00:02:00.710
to me and then when I find out they are not
interesting to anyone else, I’ll give it

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:07.620
to 10 key people and I’ll see what is the
consensus of what is working and what is not.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.140
Is the screenplay slow?

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.670
Which character is not needed?

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.390
Can I take two characters and combine them?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:22.660
I’ll do that stuff until I give it to my
inner circle of people who I think are smart

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.220
and trust.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.001
Bouncing a screenplay is very important (off
of people) and I feel I have the ability to

00:02:30.001 --> 00:02:30.430
do that.

